/validation_and_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JW84N7721S0PCYD/prj_1KRAVH8Y81S0WQ8Z/pjd_1M14DKQ031S01HV9/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JW84N7721S0PCYD/prj_1KRAVH8Y81S0WQ8Z/pjd_1KXQXFR9J1S0CWF4/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JW84N7721S0PCYD/prj_1KRAVH8Y81S0WQ8Z/pjd_1KWV98CF51S0TGRJ/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\n200Y+\\nProject Bhumisara\\nEarthrevive Technologies\\nISSUED\\n2,089.21\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n01 Feb 2026 to 01 Feb 2036\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nThe project is being implemented is co-located with an industrial partner, where we have deployed two gasifiers. The existing industrial unit utilizes the generated energy, while biochar is produced as a co-product. The biochar is subsequently distributed to farmers for soil application, thereby enabling long-term CO₂ sequestration.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\nCarbon Check\\n->\\nProject code\\nKQX6\\nApproval date\\n28 Aug 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nProject Bhumisara\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n06 Jul 2026\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 2,089.21 tCO₂e removed from Project Bhumisara on 30 Jun 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n2,089.208 t\\nSequestrations\\n2,449.945 t\\n-\\nActivities\\n360.737 tCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n28 Aug 2026\\tValidation and Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n28 Aug 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n17 Jul 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n06 Jul 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 4 of 4\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n2,089.21\\nRetired\\n0\\nCrediting period\\n01 Feb 2026 to 01 Feb 2036\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tSupplier allocation\\n28 Aug 2026\\t2,089.21\\t2,089.21\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as no observable risk. No certificates from this project are allocated to a buffer pool.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"